hi hello~
The forrestal bows and winks at you.  'G'day.  How do you do?  Welcome to
the &+Wgroves&n.  What may I do for you?'
~
M
groves~
'The groves?'  He pats a nearby tree fondly.  'This used to be a small
garden patch in my backyard ages ago.  It seems to have outgrown its small
confines,' he chuckles.  'I plant the trees and take care of the animals.
I watch what happens in the grove and keep tabs on those that live here.'
~
M
fairy~
'The fairies are wonderful people.  A little simple, perhaps, but it is the
simple that enjoy life the most.'
~
M
sprite~
The forrestal nods slowly.  'They are new here.  They appeared a little
while, when one of my favorite groves turned &+Wdark and twisted&n.'  The
forrestal sighs sadly.  'There are four varieties, and they hang out in
different groves.  There are earth sprites, water, fire and air sprites.'
~
M
earth~
'I like these fellows,' the forrestal chuckles.  'They take after my own
heart with their love for the earth.  I think they may be moving on, to see
the world.  But they will be back.  Who knows?  Perhaps I will choose my
own successor from them.'
~
M
water~
'Nice ladies,' he chuckles drily, 'if a little emotional at times.  They
dance well.  When they move,' he says, his eyes going far away, 'it is like
water moving.  Fluid and graceful ... '  He give a small little laugh and
wipes a tear from the corner of his eye.
~
M
fire~
The forrestal's face grows dark with anger.  'These I do not like.  I wish
them gone from the vale as quickly as possible.  I hate the flame that
kills, and those arrogant scum are careless.'
~
M
air~
'They're nice.  A little limited in the sense, perhaps,' he laughs, 'but
nice just the same.'
~
M
brownie~
'Shy ones, these are.  You managed to see some of them?  They don't talk
much, even to me.'
~
M
koala~
'I have no idea how these fellows came to the grove.  I planted some trees,
and the next season they were climbing them.  I like them though -- they're
