~
M
dark twisted~
'There was once a grove of rowan trees there,' he said.  'There is
something naturally magical about them.  Perhaps I should not have planted
so many of them close together.  I think that is what did it.  Opened the
dimensional &+Wrift&n, that is.'
~
M
rift~
'A great rift was opened, or rather, I should say,' he said drily, 'torn
into the fabric of reality.  For a while things were utter chaos, until I
managed to seal the fragments of the elemental planes away.  But the
&+Wrowans&n were horribly changed, and the grove beyond the rowans can be
dangerous indeed.  If you are not careful, you will end up in one of the
rifts!'
~
M
rowans~
The forrestal grows sad.  'These were the favorite amongst all the trees.
There is something magical about them, I tell you.  I wish there was some
way I could &+Wheal&n them.'
~
M
heal~
The forrestal sighs a large sigh.  'I don't know.  Nothing I've tried has
worked; the damage was done by magical powers far beyond this realm.  I
need something as powerful and as otherworldly to fix it.  I've tried
everything else.  This is the last thing I can think of.'
~
M
element elemental~
'Hmm?  What's that?  I'm not sure what you're asking, but I remember a
verse from a long, long time ago ....'  The forrestal's eyes grow distant
and preoccupied for a moment.  'It went something like:

                     First is earth, sturdy and firm,
                       Next is water, eater of all,
                              Air the empty,
                      Fire the quick, always hungry.'

The forrestal pauses.  'There is more to it,' he says, brow furrowed, then
continues haltingly,

                    'Ether the binder, mix of them all
                and Void the missing, the unfillable hole.'

The forrestal grins.  'Didn't know I still knew that.'
~
Q
The forrestal takes the box and his eyes grow wide with wonder.  'I was
told once, long, long ago about a substance like this.  I might be able to
use this to heal my grove!  Thank you, brave adventurer!'  He casts about
as if looking for something.  'Well hmm.  I must, as a matter of honor,
repay you for your service.  Take this earring!  It will serve you well in
the different worlds you may wander.'
~
