weapons~
"Ah, yes. Weapons. That's my trade, you know. I make the finest weapons in
Sarmiz'Duul. Do you know why?" he asks.

He waits patiently.

"Because I'm the only weaponsmith in town!" He roars with laughter and digs
his knuckles into your ribs.

"Seriously, now. Weapons making isn't what it used to be.  There was a time
when I had materials running out of my ears. Nowadays, it's getting harder
and harder to find obsidian in any decent quality. In fact, I'm working on
a dagger for my daughter, and I can't find even a sliver of obsidian that's
good enough quality to use in a gift for her."

He sighs.

"Maybe if you find some obsidian, you could bring it to me? Yes?" He looks
at you expectantly.
~
Q
"Ah.. this is exactly what I'm looking for!" he says happily.

He rummages through his pile of weapons and compares it to a half-forged
dagger.

"Perfect," he says, " Hmm.. what can I give you for this."

He spends a good 10 minutes rummaging around his store before grabbing an
item.

"Here, this was brought to me by some beggar. At first, I thought it was
a good quality weapon, but I have since discovered the balance is all wrong,
and it is made from substandard metals. But, I'm sure you could give it to
a friend as a costume weapon, or maybe sell it for a few copper."
~
