M
severne~
"Ah.. Severne," he sighs.

"Let me tell you a story of a foolish half-orc who once vied for the hand
of the most beautiful creature this side of Hades.  He courted her, wooed
her, showered her with fine stolen gifts.  He even managed to drag her
away from her former love, an ugly, clumsy and stupid warrior.  Then, one
day, he let himself get sold on a deal that forced him to rob her.  He
used his familiarity with her to get into her personal vault and steal an
elixir for a mage from Tharnadia.  She found out, of course (never trust
that women won't find out), and she threw him and his heart out into the
street.  He knew that she still wanted him, but she refused him unless he
made up somehow for his mistake."

He sighs again.

"This half-orc managed to acquire the formula for a potion she has been
researching for most of her life, one that will cause the drinker to have
permanent infravision.  But, she won't even talk to him now, and sends his
couriers back to him without even listening to what he has to say."

He continues, "And to top it off, I can't even find my dagger. With nothing
left of my pride, I cannot bear to live another day."

He buries his head in his hands.
~
M
dagger~
"Oh, I'm sure one of my students took it as a show of skill to his peers.
