M
regulars~
"The Regulars were formed many years ago by the First King, Destper.  He
wanted to have a military force separate from the local militia and the army
that was dedicated to no king, no land, and no leader other than their own
for protection of the city.  A group that could not be bought, because they
had no wants.  Well, things have changed in the last hundred years, and we
are the effective police force now.  The peacekeepers are a good lot," he
gestures at one in the distance, "but not very well trained.  Sometimes, we
have to drag them out of the bar after a night of drinking and threatening
some poor SOB with punishment unless he pays for a drink. "

He sighs.

"You know, I've always said that the peacekeepers just need a symbol or
leader or something to give them purpose.  Perhaps a statue, hm, or some
sort of weapon, a sword even."

He ponders.

"If you happen across anything that could be of use to my problem, then
please, bring it to me."

He straightens his tunic.

"Well, I need to get back to my duties. It's been a pleasure talking to you.
I hope I don't have to meet you later under less agreeable circumstances."

He bows and turns away.
~
M
sword~
"A sword? You know, if I had a sword that was of unique manufacture,
preferably one that was ancient.. a relic, that might be enough to help them.
They need to feel like they are doing something valuable, and protecting an
ancient sword of questionable heritage just might do it." He smiles.
~
Q
"Perfect!  This sword has just enough rust and weakness of metal to be a
perfect symbol."

He thanks you heartily.

"Here.. let me see what I can give you as payment."

After a fruitless search about his person, he pulls a small bag from his
pouch.

"I know it's not much, but I found this a few days ago. I have no idea what
it is, other than it's magical.  Perhaps you can find some use for it."

He brushes his cloak out of the way as he starts to hand it to you.

"Wait, here, take my cloak as well.  It's been a good friend over the last
few years, and perhaps it can serve you as well as it has served me.  Again,
I thank you for your help."

He salutes, and turns away.
~
