"Oh, I enjoy being the advisor to the King.  It is my whole purpose in
life," he says loudly, while glancing at the King.  He motions you closer.

"I hate this job," he whispers, "and the first chance I get to make a
'vertical advancement' I will.  As a matter of fact, I am right now working
on a spell to put.."

He coughs and glances at Rodev.

"Put a certain adversary in a permanent coma that not even Tavril himself
could break him from.  But, sadly, I am missing some key ingredients, and
a part of the forumla eludes me."

He sighs.

"Perhaps we can do each other a favor. I need a demons heart, a small amount
of the Dust of Binding, a potion of sleep, and some clue to the rest of the
spell.  If you can bring me these things, I will be willing to give you an
item of great power.. the only thing of power that I have.  Think about it."

He turns back and stands next to his King.
~
Q
"YES!! You have found the items I need to complete my spell.  The king will
fall into a coma, and I will use my powers as a mage to 'communicate' with
him to do his will.  The Kingdom is MINE!!"

He suddenly looks furtive, and regains his composure.

"I must first *make* the potion, then give it to the King, then see if it
works, and THEN I can celebrate.  Remember your training," he says to
himself.  He looks back to you.

"Here, I give to you the last item of real power I have.  And hopefully I
will need."

He smiles.
~
