sarmiz'duul sarmiz~
"Sarmiz'Duul.. what a dreary place.  I have been the diplomat here for nearly
20 years, and I have yet to settle on a treaty with these half-mongrels."

He grumbles.

"To make things worse, even at night when I can get out of this dull room
and wander the streets, there are none of my kind that I may pass the time
with.  Every time I try to just keep to myself, or quietly have a drink, some
drunk overgrown pig in an official uniform starts reciting false city laws
stating that all drow within the city after nightfall must buy a round."

He growls, and his eyes spark.

"I cannot do anything against these morons, for it would destroy what little
I have accomplished these long two decades.. but if someone were to bring me
proof that one of these questionable men had met an untimely fate, say a token
that proves their occupation, I would reward the person handsomely."

He smiles wickedly.
~
Q
The drow throws back his head laughs long and hard.

"Ah.. this is a good day for me.  I haven't felt this good since I last
killed an illithid.  I thank you for this."

He smiles and turns away.

"Oh, yes, the matter of payment. I have something here you might like.  I
took this scroll from a half-breed grey several years ago.  I am not familiar
with this particular magical writing, nor do I have the access to the Father
Guild that I once did.  Perhaps you can have it deciphered, and you can find
some value in it. No refunds."

He bites his lower lip.

"Let me make you a deal.  Here is another scroll I have.  One that will allow
you to spy on those that you may be suspicious of.  I will give you this
as additional payment, on the condition that you kill another one or two of
those bags of slime in uniform.  No need to prove it.. just kill them."

He smiles wickedly.
~
