#13501
M
hello hi name~
The archer smiles at you warmly, and says "Welcome to our woods. My name
is Farlindel, and this is my brother, Hanson."
~
M
woods forest~
"Well actually," he says, "the woods are not technically ours.  They belong
to the twin mages who live in the tower.  But we are allowed to reside here
in exchange for providing the tower residents with fresh game, as well as
tanned hides and furs."
~
M
game~
"Yes," he says warmly, "the woods are plentiful with game.  Nevertheless,
I'd be very careful killing anything if I were you, unless you have been
given permission to do so.  The mages don't look too kindly upon poaching
in here."
~
M
mage mages brothers tower~
Farlindel looks serious for a moment, then says, 'Well, they are a bit
strange, you know.  Very powerful, I have no doubt, but there's something
just a little strange about them. Take my advice and stay away from there."
~
M
archer~
Farlindel fairly glows with pride as he tells you, "Yes, I am an archer.  We
were taught by our father to use a bow almost before we could walk.  When we
are not actually hunting, we love to come here to the range and practice."
~
M
practice~
Farlindel looks a bit irritated.  He sighs deeply, then says, "Thing is, we
seem to be spending more time hunting our arrows lately, than hunting game,
or target shooting, for that matter.  Those damn woodland sprites!"
~
M
sprites~
Farlindel chuckles a bit, then says, "Well, I suppose it is kinda funny, I
know they are just being playful, they are such fun-loving creatures.  But
it is just so irritating, nevertheless.  See, they keep stealing our arrows,
and hiding them in the woods, burying them deep into the underbrush.  And it
is so time-consuming to have to go and find them all."  He looks thoughtful
for a moment, looks you over carefully, then says, "Hmm, perhaps you would
like to help us out, and bring our arrows to us?"
~
M
arrows arrow~
Farlindel says "Sure, we don't have much, but we could pay you at least a
little bit for each of our arrows you recover for us.  Just bring them here,
we are bound to be here sooner or later.  You can tell our arrows from the
rest by the blue feathers on a green shaft."
~
