M
hello hi name~
The archer smiles at you warmly, and says "Well hello there, and welcome to
our woods.  My name is Hanson, and this is my brother, Farlindel."
~
M
woods forest~
"Well actually," he says, "the woods are not technically ours.  They belong
to the twin mages who live in the tower.  But our family has lived here for
several generations, as we provide the tower residends with fresh game, and
tanned hides and furs from our hunting."
~
M
game~
"Well," he says warmly, "the woods are plentiful with game.  However, you
must know how to properly prepare it if you want to get anything edible from
it."
~
M
hide hides fur furs skin~
Hanson contemplates for a moment, then says, 'Well, tell you what.  If you
were to bring us some freshly killed game, and were also willing to pay us a
small fee for our time, we could replace your game with fresh meat from our
own supply, as well as the appropriate skin or fur.  You see, it takes time
to properly prepare skins and furs, and we have the expertise.  But we would
need a replacement for anything we were to let you have."
~
M
archer~
Hanson fairly glows with pride as he tells you, "Yes, our father taught us
to use a bow very young in life."
~
M
father~
Hanson smiles warmly, and says, "Our father lives on the other side of the
woods from here.  He and our mother have a nice little cottage there, where
they grow vegetables to accompany the fresh game from the forest.  My mother
also makes some very nice clothing from the skins and furs.  You should go
see her if you'd like some made."
~
M
mother~
Hanson smiles warmly.  "Yes," he says, "Mother is very good with the needle.
She made all the clothes my brother and I are wearing."
~
