hello hi howdy name~
The hermit blinks, surprised, and looks up, seeming to take notice
of your presence for the first time.

"Ahem, why, howdy there, young'n." he sputters, then pauses a moment,
as though thinking.

Studying you closely, he finally says, "If'n you could get me a nice
batch a' wood, that'd be mighty good of ya.  I ain't been able to do
much lately, and the huntin' round here just seems to get worse 'n
worse as time goes on..  All's I needs is a little kindling and some
nice chunks a' wood that'd burn nice 'n proper."

With that, he resumes staring off into space.
~
M
hunting hunt~
Squinting at you, the hermit explains, "Yes'n, used ta be could get some
good game round here.  Ain't no more though, ain't no more..  Iss' all
been scared off by them strange goins'-on near the graveyard."

At that, he stops, apparently lost in thought.
~
M
graveyard strange scared tomb~
The old man suddenly becomes very animated, leaping to his feet and
pointing a bony finger at you.  "You liss'n up, young'n, if'n yer
thinkin' of checkin' it out, you had best watch out!  I ain't gonna
be no party to killin' some silly young'ns..."

The life drained out of him, he slumps back down onto his bed.
~
Q
The old man looks at you, happy and mildly surprised.

"Been a long time since anyone did sumth'n to help me, young'n." he says,
practically glowing.  "Liss'n, I ain't never told many people this, but
sumth'n real strange is goin' on over at that graveyard, ya hear me?  I
used ta' have a key to onna them tombs, but ever since all this
strangeness, I ain't trusted it."

He pauses for a moment, deeply in thought.

"I thinks I threw it someplace on the eastern part a' that trail that
rings the graveyard.  Ya know it, of course ya do, ya got here, right?"

For a few long seconds, he laughs at his own joke (much too loudly), then
finally stops when a coughing fit wracks his skinny frame.

"Well, again I thank ya, young'n.  Ya really helped out an old coot."
~
