hi hello quest help hail~
The paladin smiles at you sadly
"The bandit scum found here have troubled Winterhaven for some time
now and their latest acts -- kidnapping the son and daughter of a
Winterhaven lord prompted the decision to raid this camp.  I was
commissioned to lead that raid.  But the foul bandits number too many
and their leader, Isoril, is too powerful.  Rather than risk the life of
more of my men, I ordered them to withdraw back to Winterhaven.

For me to return to Winterhaven as well is unthinkable -- living with
such a blow to my honor is a fate worse than death.

Adventurer you can help!  You can enter the camp under the guise of a slave
trader.  The bandits won't recognize you as a threat and you will be able
to move freely within the camp.

I have three missions for you:  Rescue the &+Wboy&N and rescue the &+Wgirl&N.
I have a &+Wkill&N task for you as well.  Ask me about either of these
missions for more information.
~
M
boy~
The son of Winterhaven Lord Perrin was kidnapped several weeks
ago by Isoril with a ransom demand of 4000 platinum coins.  The ransom
was not paid and I fear the worst, particularly after the failed raid.
Enter the camp, find where he is being held captive and bring him to me.
It may be too late -- if it is, at least show me proof.  Give me his ring.
The ring is pure gold, very ornate and very valuable.  Perhaps  the
bandits are still keeping it in their possession.  Go!  You will be well
rewarded.
~
M
girl~
Lord Perrin's daughter was kidnapped several weeks ago
along with Perrin's son.  I have learned that Perrin's daughter may still
be alive and may be prisoner in Isoril's personal quarters!  Isoril is
an anti-paladin of incredible power.  You will not be able to defeat him,
but, if you possess skills of stealth then you don't have to!  Try sneaking
into his quarters and see if Perrin's daughter is being held there.  If she
is, unlock her shackles and set her free.  I am sure Isoril keeps the key
to her shackles somewhere in his quarters, possibly his desk...
~
M
kill~
The full members of Isoril's inner circle identify themselves
with a blood red tear insignia.  If these members were slain, it would
cause chaos with Isoril's ranks and possibly leave them open to a raid
that would wipe out the bandit camp for good.  Slay these full members
and bring me their insignias as proof.  You will be rewarded.
