and his hammer. "I fought side by side with Khildarak in many battles, a
fierce warrior was he. I have seen with my own eyes the wonderment that his
hammer created, it seemed to make him invinceable. The mines in which he was
killed are rumored to be below the stronghold somewhere. The duergar that
know where the entrance to these mines is located are tight lipped indeed,
as the ones that have entered them have never returned. Most think that the
mines are now inaccesible due to the great cave in. The excitment for the
hunt of the bone that unlocks the case of the hammer has faded with time.
