#17248
M
bones bone mine~
The Kuo-Tao priest looks puzzled and thinks for a few moments. "I have found
some old mine tunnels on my way to this place, they appear to have once been
above the water, but now are submerged. There was one area in particular that
had many bones lying about the bottom. I could not determine the race of the
creatures that the bones belonged to and indeed did take a small piece of a
bone in hopes one of the more experienced member of my tribe may be able to
tell. Your interest in my piece of bone suprises me, as it seems very common
and ordinary to me. I would be willing to part with the bone if you will do
a task that would aid me and my commorades."
~
M
hello hi greetings~
The Kuo-Tao priest looks relieved at your words. "Greetings strange looking
being. I was so affraid that you were not friendly, having to fight in this
cramped cavern would only add more grief to our already grief filled journey.
We have been trapped here for a long time, unable to return to our village."
~
M
journey trapped~
The Kuo-Tao priest lets a small sigh escape from its huge fish mouth. "We left
our village some time ago on a small expedition of exploration. We encountered
a cavern full of giant Kraken and had to flee past them as they had blocked
the way we had came. We then encountered a small tribe of ixitxachitl and chose
to fight on through their home tunnels rather than go back and face the kraken.
When we found this small cavern we were near death, we have been here ever
since trying to think of a way to get back to our village."
~
M
kraken krakens~
The Kuo-Tao priest nods his head slightly. "We found this giant cavern we
thought to be previously undiscovered. In our excitement we entered the
cavern without first scouting it for safety. The kraken attacked quickly,
I believe there were two of them, I cannot be sure. We were caught near the
opposite wall that we had entered and were forced to flee in this direction.
Be very carefull when exploring this area."
~
M
task~
The Kuo-Tao priest lowers his head slightly as he speaks. "I am affraid the
task I require is a great one, the prize of this small piece of bone is hardly
worthy of the greatness that would be required to complete it. However, our
situation is desparate, as we long to be home in our village. We can make it
through the ixitxachitls on our own, but would be weakened severly by the
time we reach the cavern of the krakens. The risk of trying to swim quickly
across the cavern to the exit that will take us back to our village is to
great. If you can find a way to destroy the krakens and allow us to go home
I will gladly give you the piece of bone you requested. Bring me proof that
the krakens have indeed been killed and the bone shall be yours. We have
blocked the tunnel that leads to the kraken cavern with a large rock, you
must shove this rock out of the way to unblock the passage to the cavern.
May your gods be with you, I hope to see you again."
~
Q
The Kuo-Tao priest looks at you in amazement and says "You have killed the
Krakens! Now we can finally get back to our village, for this we are most
gratefull. Here is the object I promised you, though I do not understand
why you would want such an ordinary object in return for a great deed. It
has been an honor to deal with a creature such as yourself. May the gods
look upon thee in favor on all your adventures."
~
