&+L                                &N
&+L   I once knew a great warrior named &+rTarl&+L, he was almost without equal in any&N
&+Lact you could imagine.  His power was legendary even for a &+Chuman&+L, I knew him&N
&+Lvery well.  He was to marry my daughter, she went to go live with her mother&N
&+Lyears ago in another kingdom.  I went there to see him, never did I see a man&N
&+Lwith more &+Rdesire &+Land drive then I met that day.  The day I arrived they had a&N
&+Lcelebration, much jousting and other battles with weapons.  He won almost all&N
&+Lthe contests without any problem, that is all except for one battle.  When he&N
&+Llost, a look came over his face that I have never seen upon anothers within my&N
&+Llong lifetime.  His &+re&+Ry&+re&+Rs &+Lturned to fire, he could not handle that he had not&N
&+Lbeen perfect.  Something inside him must of snapped that day, the competitions&N
&+Llasted for nine days.  This happened the first day of the tournament, as each&N
&+Lday passed he became more and more aggressive.  He won all the events for the&N
&+Lnext three days without any defeat.  The fifth day had arrived, on that day he&N
&+Llost again to the same person, the name of the warrior escapes me at this time&N
&+Lall I remember is he is suppose to own a &+ytavern &+Lor a bar these days.  When he&N
&+Llost again that same look returned only with more anger and hatred then I can&N
&+Lever explain with feeble words.  The six day arrived, he had all but lost it,&N
&+Lhis battles almost turned into inhuman slaughters.  He nearly killed at least&N
&+Lnine of the knights that he faced that day, yet again he lost the tenth battle&N
&+Lto the same warrior again.  This really pushed him over the edge, day eight&N
&+Lrolled around and his anger was without control.  His ninth fight he not only&N
&+Lwon but he had to be stopped by my daughter, or he might of killed the knight.&N
&+LAgain he faced the same fighter, he attacked with rage and hatred, wild like a&N
&+Lbull fighting a matador almost.  His humanity almost seemed like it had left,&N
&+Lhe lost again, that really did not sit well with him.  The stare of dread that&N
&+LI saw within his eyes was not meant for any to ever have to see.  He screamed&N
&+Land swore that the final day he would win all the matches or die trying.  The&N
&+Lman that kept defeating him gazed at him and smiled and &+wwhispered &+Lthese words&N
&+L'&+wOnly Death is Real&+L' after speaking he simply turned around and walked away.&N
&+LThe final day had arrived, again &+rTarl &+Ldestroyed the first nine knights that he&N
&+Lfaced, almost killing a few of them in his wake.  Everything seemed to be the&N
&+Lsame as it had been, yet something was different about &+rTarl&+L.  Losing control&N
&+Lwas already normal for him, this day however it was something more, his soul&N
&+Lwas tainted.  The fight started, he was losing again, each blow that he struck&N
&+Lthat missed or failed to harm would only get him more angered.  He started to&N
&+Lswing wild, his control and training totally lost, he took a solid shot that&N
&+Lwould of laid almost any other man to rest.  The strike only stunned the beast&N
&+Lfor a second, suddenly his &+Reyes &+Lglowed red with dread, his helm seemed almost&N
&+Lto move from the top of his head alone.  He started to win for a while, he was&N
&+Lalmost ready to finish off the knight that had defeated him so many times.  I&N
&+Ldo not know why but he hesitated for a second, that was all the other knight&N
&+Lneeded to react.  He tripped &+rTarl &+Land asked him to yield, with some protest he&N
&+Lrelented.  The knight had won with honor, even with his humanity lost &+rTarl &+Ldid&N
&+Lnot dispute what had happened.  That was the last time anyone saw &+rTarl&+L, crazed&N
&+Lrumors and stories have been told of him since.  What has truly happened none&N
&+Lreally know, I know it is odd but something about the &+cshaman &+Lreminds me of the&N
&+Lgreat warrior I have just spoke of.  Sorry If I rambled so long, I am old all&N
&+LI really have left are memories of the past that create my paradise.&N
~
