in his hands. With deliberate slowness, he removes his hat,
setting it gently on the ground, then peels away a painted mask
that has concealed him all this time. Beneath it is the face of a
seasoned scholar, hunted and relentless, with scars that speak of
countless battles.

&+C'I am not merely Rictavio the charlatan some fools take me for.
&+CI am Rudolph van Richten, monster hunter, chronicler of the cursed,
&+Cand scourge of vampires. I have walked the shadowed paths of this
&+Cvalley for decades, hunting horrors that would drive most mad.'

&NHe pauses, letting the words settle, then prudces a small &+Ykey&N.
&+C'This key... unlocks the gate to my tower, my sanctuary, my laboratory
&+Cof knowledge and strategy. There, I keep the tools and secrets
&+Cnecessary to ensure that creatures like Strahd never rise again.'

&+C'Take it,' &+CRudolph Van Richten &Ncontinues &+C'and there we will plan
&+Cwhat comes next - Barovia will not heal itself and I cannot do it alone.'
