your eyes, as if his vision was slightly skewed to one side.

At the very moment you are convinced he will say no more, he blurts out
something almost incomprehensable..

He says 'After speaking with the book, it was very clear he was not happy
where he was, in that cold castle.
I simply could'nt leave him with that barbaric bafoon!
he did'nt even have the common courtesy to read him once in a while, a truly
desperate situation I could not ignore. He has a new home, where he is
loved, and kept warm! He's very old you know, he can't be exposed to the
cold of the north anymore, lest his pages disintigrate.'
