M
keep history~
&+wVarathorn &+Lspeaks:&N
&+w
&+w   Yes, I shall tell you the history of this keep, for I am the former master&N
&+wof it.  I am not sure where the best part is to start all this, I suppose the&N
&+wlessons of youth are not always learned.&N
&+w
&+w   I was once a great warrior, without an equal.  That was not good enough for&N
&+wme.  I wanted more, I needed more, I had to rule, I longed for power.  I could&N
&+wnot risk failure so I invoked dark forces to help me.  I always thought my&N
&+wblade could deal death out to any feeble magician.  I thought I was the one who&N
&+wwas doing the using.  I conquered kingdoms with ease, slayed many in my wake,&N
&+wI did not care for anyone but myself.  The more I gained the less I seemed to&N
&+weven realize or care.  Any who dared to get in my way were smited, I had taken&N
&+wover nearly all the lands.  The world was within my grasp, I was so close to&N
&+wjust having it all.  Any thing I desired was mine, women, wine, treasures, it&N
&+wwas all in my hands.  Finally I had gotten what I truly wanted, true power.  I&N
&+wshould of stopped while I was ahead of the game.  For I had served the forces&N
&+wwell enough to of been allowed to enjoy my conquest.  Yet I pushed for more and&N
&+wmore power.  Until I would stop at nothing to be Immortal.  No matter what it&N
&+wwould take I was prepared.  Some tried to reason with me, I had them beheaded&N
&+wand impaled upon spikes.  My soul was already lost, I summoned up a force that&N
&+wwas beyond any I had ever seen before.  This being spoke to me about an eternal&N
&+wdeal that would grant me what I wished for.&N
&+w
&+w   The deal was that I'd live forever and never die as long as my soul was kept&N
&+win a mystical ossuary.  That seemed more than fair to me at the time.  I should&N
&+wof suspected something, the being wanted nothing in return.  Little did I know&N
&+wthat I was about to pay a price none should never have to.&N
&+w                                                                   &N
&+w   I accepted the deal, and yes I am immortal.  Yet it is really a wicked curse&N
&+wnone should ever have to endure.  For I can not die, I shall always rise back&N
&+wup.  At the same time I continue to age, I have been alive for centuries, I am&N
&+win so much pain it can not be put into words.  My hands ache everyday of my&N
&+wdismal life.  Not one second passes without me feeling pain beyond words.  I&N
&+wwould do anything to gain my final release.  Sometimes I think the worst part&N
&+wis how I doomed everyone within the keep.  For I made another foolish deal and&N
&+wthats how this keep came to this dreary place.  Their souls in exchange for my&N
&+wfreedom.  He kept his word in a twisted way.&N
&+w                                                                       &N
&+w   I am bound to this room, I can not enter the tower because of the mystical&N
&+wwards within the place.  He did however place the ossuary in another place&N
&+wbesides his wicked chamber.  I dare not speak his name, for if he heard it he&N
&+wwould surely come here and torture me again.  Please bring me the ossuary so&N
&+wthat I may have my freedom.  The souls within this domain are already lost, at&N
&+wleast allow me my release.  They no longer feel pain at least, do this for me&N
&+wand I shall reward you with the badge I once wore into battle.&N
&+w
~
Q
&+wVarathorn &+Lspeaks:&N

&+w   You have done very well, now at last I can have my eternal rest.  I never&N
&+wthought this day would come.&N
~
