map gc level experience~
&+WThis map on the desk is plenty big enough for us both to look at it at once.
&+WI've done a lot of travelling and marked interesting places along with some
&+Wnotes about each at the bottom.  If you are just now setting out looking for
&+Wadventure I would suggest you check out Ako.  It is a pretty tame forest, but
&+Wyou can find some adventure there to get started with.  Just be sure to pay
&+Wattention to the guards in the area.  They are peaceful enough, but if they
&+Wcatch you abusing one of their people they will attack without mercy!  If you
&+Wcan find me some &+Ypaper&n I can try and make a copy of my map you can take with
&+Wyou.  I bet the innkeeper keeps some in the desk in the library down the hall.&n

&+WI may be getting ahead of myself though, &+YTharnadia&+W is a pretty big and
&+Wconfusing place by itself.  Are you comfortable getting around?  If not, I'm not
&+Wthat busy,just ask and I'm glad to help!&n
~
MA
tharnadia directions~
&+WDon't feel bad about getting lost around here, everyone does!
&+WI've been here dozens of times and even I have to stick to the
&+Wmain roads, or I'd be lost myself.  This inn is in a good
&+Wlocation though.  The fountain outside marks pretty much the
&+Wcenter of town.  There are a few shops within walking distance
&+Wif you find some items to sell, or want to buy some new and
&+Wstronger gear for your travels.  If you are ready to leave town
&+Wjust follow the Great Bazaar east of the inn, and keep following
&+Wthat path east until you leave the city limits.  From there you
&+Wshould be able to find your way, especially if you take a look at
&+Wmy &+Ymap&+W before you go.  If you get lost you can always ask
&+Wother adventurers, but beware, outside of the city not all of the
&+Wadventurers you meet will be friendly!&n
~
MA
search bag instruments play music~
&+WYou can never be too careful when staying at a crowded inn.
&+WYou never know who is sneaking around so I can't leave my
&+Winstruments in plain view.  I hide them under things in my
&+Wbag to help make sure nobody steals them, but I don't mind
&+Wif you want to play them for a while.  Just &+Ysearch&+W that
&+Wbag a little and you should find them easily enough.  If you
&+Whave a specific instrument you like to play just keep searching
&+Wtil you find the one you like.&n
~
M
bard profession~
&+WInterested in bards are you?  I bet you've heard bards referred to
&+Was jacks-of-all-trades before?  It's true.  Why devote all your time
&+Wto one discipline the way all of the other professions do?  It's all
&+Wabout versatility.  Warriors, sorcerors, clerics, and all the others
&+Whave their strengths, but all are also doomed by obvious weaknesses.
&+WWarriors can endure a lot of punishment in battle, but eventually
&+Wtheir vitality runs out.  Clerics can continually refresh themselves,
&+Wbut being unable to damage their attacks they can only survive, never
&+Wwin.  Us bards realized that we needed to learn a bit of everything to
&+Wbest survive, instead of a lot of just one thing.  We can fight, we can
&+Wcast magic, and we can even heal a little.  We can come and go stealthily
&+Wwithout anyone else knowing, or we can weave enchantments over friend
&+Wand foe alike with mystifying melodies from our instruments.  We are
&+Wmasters of adaptation, being able to respond to any situation we encounter!&n
~
