#132660
MA
advice~
&+WIt is good that you are not too proud to ask for advice from others,
&+Wyou'll learn a lot from people that have experienced things before you.
&+WA lot of young fighters are disillusioned and think fighting is all
&+Wabout charging your enemy fearlessly and trying to hack them to pieces,
&+Wbut it is so much more than that.  Charging opponents recklessly will
&+Wquickly get you killed.  Effective fighting requires careful thought.
&+WBefore attacking, &+Yconsider&+W your enemy.  That will help you judge
&+Wyour ability to win.  If the odds look bad, leave to develop your skills
&+Wmore fully before you return.  Likewise, in the midst of battle itself,
&+Wthe main focus should not be on delivering mortal blows, but defending
&+Wyourself from the blows of your enemy.  Expensive armors can help you
&+Wsurvive the occasional blow, but not even mithril can save you against
&+Wrepeated onslaught.  Therefore, develop your skills so that you can
&+Wnimbly dodge most attacks, and parry or riposte the others.  Those
&+Wskills will do more for you than any amount of armor.&n
~
