adventure adventures memoirs travels story stories~
&+yL&+Ye&+Wo&+yd&+Yra&n's face brightens as he sits back and begins reciting his heroics.

	&+W"That bullywug chieftain was tough, let me tell you.  By some stroke of luck
	&+Won his part, he managed to withstand my mighty chill touch and charged me
	&+Wbefore I could conjure another.  My companions, not grasping the extent of my
	&+Wpower to defend myself, ran to my rescue and insisted I stay behind them during
	&+Wsuch intense battles.  Although I saw it as unneccesary, I decided to humor them
	&+Wby letting them stay in front and feel important for once.  I didn't need to engage
	&+Wthe enemy with my weapons, I could sit back and let the warrior and ranger fight it,
	&+Wwhile I sat behind and hurled my spells at it safely.

&+yL&+Ye&+Wo&+yd&+Yra&n's smile begins to fade as he notices you don't look impressed.  He hurriedly launches into another heroic adventure.

	&+W"Well, this other time we journeyed into a rather secluded wood in the great land of
	&+WEvermeet.  We had gone a ways before we realized we couldn't hear the sounds of any
	&+Wwildlife, and alerted to a possible trap.  Immediately we were charged from every side
	&+Wby a fierce group of urd warriors.  One of our wizards fell immediately from an arrow
	&+Wbefore our warriors jumped in front to protect the other casters.  Our other wizard
	&+Wbegan blasting them with alternate bursts of fire and ice, while our druid slammed ones
	&+Wthat got too close with fists of stone and strong currents of wind.  I assisted them by
	&+Wsummoning my own bursts of frigid ice, yet they shouted at me to stop that and instead
	&+Wenchant our faltering warriors.  Personally I thought that was our cleric's job, but he
	&+Wjust wasn't powerful enough to keep the healing going fast enough.  So even though my
	&+Wspells could have helped kill them and end the encounter quickly, I had to instead
	&+Wcontinually cast &+Lstone skin&n on the tanks so they wouldn't fall.  If they had been
	&+Wstronger and better trained they wouldn't have needed my constant help, though I suppose
	&+Wwhen you choose to travel with lesser adventurers you should be prepared to drop what you
	&+Ware doing and look after them."&n

Seeing that you are still not impressed, his face flushes and he turns away from you again.

	&+W"I am very busy.  If you cannot find a book I can use please go away and come
	&+Wback another time."&n
~
