	&+W"I had been tailing a rich merchant for some time. Not long ago he
	&+Wstole a golden pendant, a family heirloom of mine, claiming it was
	&+Wpayment for a debt I owed him.  I saved up enough money to pay him
	&+Win order to get it back, yet he refused, saying that it was too late,
	&+Wand that if I really wanted it back the interest would increase the
	&+Wamount to ten times what I originally owed.  I cannot come up with
	&+Wthat amount of money, nor do I think I should have to.  He had no
	&+Wright to take my father's pendant, and I will do whatever it takes
	&+Wto get it back!  Earlier I tried to break into his room and take it
	&+Wwhile he was out, but he returned at the last moment and his bodyguards
	&+Wgot a lucky hit on me before I escaped.  I thought I would be fine, but
	&+Wit won't stop &+Rbleeding&+W."&n
~
