race races centaur~
	&+W"You will meet a great many peoples in this city, and even more should your travels take
	&+Wyou to distant lands, such as that of the Khomani-Khan.  Each race has its strengths and
	&+Wweaknesses, and you should plan your strategy with that in mind.  I am sure you are
	&+Waccustomed to seeing the humanoid races which are common in this area of the world, such
	&+Was dwarves and gnomes and elves, but let me explain to you the differences between some
	&+Wof the other races which tend to dwell far from here, but you are sure to meet on your
	&+Wjourneys.

	&+gCen&+Ltaurs&+W, live in the forests of the far west, in the land of Evermeet, and are half horse,
	&+Wwhich makes them strong and sturdy.  Only the largest of opponents, such as &+bOgres &+Wand
	&+LMino&+rtaurs&+W can bash them to the ground, but the reverse is also true that their size also
	&+Wmakes it difficult for them to do the same to others.  Our horse-body allows us to carry our
	&+Wcompanions on our back as long as we have a saddle for them to sit on.  Our legendary stamina
	&+Wallows us to outrun any wingless opponent, and our powerful legs allow us to kick in all but
	&+Wmagically sealed doors.  However, the universal fear of dragons is also inescapable for us.
	&+WDragons prefer horse flesh to any other meal, and knowing that we would be the preferred
	&+Wtarget during battle always causes us to panic and flee.

	&+LMino&+rtaurs&+W hail from the distant forested continent of the Khomani-Khan, and are similar to
	&+Wus, gaining great strength and constitution from the half of them that are not human.  They can
	&+Wsee perfectly day or night, and their powerful legs and solid upper body make them very
	&+Weffective at charging their foe, slamming it so powerfully that it becomes momentarily paralyzed
	&+Wtrying to gather its breath and its senses.  The power of the bull is not without its drawbacks
	&+Whowever.  Just as the sight of dragons terrifies my people, physical pain infuriates the bull
	&+Winside of each &+LMino&+rtaur&+W.  After significant damage is taken, it loses control, flying
	&+Winto an insatiable rage.  Its strength and vitality climb even higher during this time, but it
	&+Wloses all ability to think and reason.  Fearing for its safety, it will charge anything near
	&+Wit which moves, even its friends, even if it were its mother or child.

	&+GThri-&+YKreens&+W dwell in the same area as the &+LMino&+rtaurs&+W, and can see in both light and
	&+Wdarkness as well, though they prefer to live in the dark in an underground city.  Their skinny and
	&+Wuniquely-shaped bodies prevent them from wearing much of the protective armor the other races use,
	&+Wbut they possess four arms to fight with!  They can wield 4 longswords, or 2 powerful broadswords,
	&+Wuse a shield and 3 swords, or any combination they choose!  Also, their evolution has gifted them
	&+Wwith a highly venomous bite, able to poison or paralyze victims that get too close to their jaws.
	&+WThough not naturally possessing great physical strength, their speed more than makes up for it.
	&+WThey are more agile and coordinated, even having innately driven dodging abilities, than nearly
	&+Wany race save &+yhalflings &+Wand &+Ggoblins&+W!

	&+yHarpies&+W dwell in the mountains to the west of the homeland of the &+Lmino&+rtaurs&+W.  They are
	&+Wan agile bird race with many unique abilities.  Strong wings allow them to remain perpetually in
	&+Wthe air, which when coupled with perfect night and day vision allows them to see a much larger area
	&+Wwhen outside than their comrades.  Isolationists by nature, the &+yharpies&+W possess many secrets
	&+Wunbeknownst to the rest of the world, such as the ability of some of them to harness the powers of
	&+Wthe stars in combat, releasing a torrent of destruction!"&n
~
