alchemy alchemist profession~
&+YN&+ye&+Ybbl&+ye&n's face lights up as you ask him about alchemy.

	&+WI am more than happy to talk with you about the art of alchemy.  It is truly
	&+Wan amazing art which is only recently beginning to be understood and taken
	&+Wseriously.  Don't listen to all the stories about witchs' cauldrons and love
	&+Wpotions and all that hocus-pocus.  Alchemy is a science, not like the magical
	&+Warts practiced by many of the other adventurers you'll meet.  A sorceror is
	&+Wable to cause an ice storm to materialize out of nothing, while a warrior is
	&+Wincapable of ever producing anything like it.  That is magic.  Alchemy is
	&+Wdifferent.  There is no need for natural power or ability.  When ingredient A
	&+Wis mixxed with ingredient B, it produces a potion with a specific effect that is
	&+Wthe same for whoever mixxes the ingredients together.  It is constant and reliable.
	&+WWith magic you sometimes fail, and at the worst times.  With alchemy it is certain.
	&+WIt will never fail you in a tight spot!"

&+YN&+ye&+Ybbl&+ye&n pauses a moment to collect his thoughts, then continues.

	&+W"Now, onto what alchemy can actually do!  The aspect of potion brewing you are
	&+Walready mildly aware of.  Potions can be brewed which neutralize potions, and some
	&+Wcan restore energy and vitality itself.  However, the power to enhance life is
	&+Wbalanced by the power also to destroy it.  Poisons can be created, as well as volatile
	&+Wacids and gasses.  Others can be made that fill you with gasses so light that it causes
	&+Wyour body to actually float!  There is more to alchemy than potion brewing however.  The
	&+Wsame concepts can be applied to metals and other materials.  Just as mixxing different
	&+Wingredients together can give potions of different effects, metals can be combined to
	&+Wproduce alloys with enhanced properties as well.  Bronze can be easily pierced.  Iron
	&+Wis more difficult, but it can be pierced as well.  However, if I melt them together I
	&+Wcan cool it into a metal that is more durable than either, and lighter as well.  I guess
	&+Wto sum it all up quickly, I can say this.  Alchemists are scientists.  They take items from
	&+Wtheir surroundings and use them to produce whatever it is they might need, be it an elixir,
	&+Wpoison, armor, or broadsword.  When a need arises, we work with what we have to address it."&n
~
