savannah~
&+g"&+wYes, yes, I'm currently looking for a place known as the Savannah of Broken
Trusts. The legend goes that M'Bele, an ancient warrior god, created a place
for his loyal followers to live in. He divided them into twenty tribes and
let them loose upon each other. Nobody knows how much time has passed since
then, but it has surely been at least five hundred years. Rumors have it that
there are only two tribes left, and when one of the surviving chieftains has
been eliminated, M'Bele himself will come to congratulate the victor.
&N   I rather hope I'm not around to see THAT happen.&+g"&N
~
M
turol~
&+g"&+wIt wasn't that long ago that I published my book on the anti-paladins of
Turol. They sparked my interest, actually, after I researched the disaster
that befell Turolopolis. Now THAT was an interesting story. The Ring of Glory
was still recovering from their war against the Raveners, and the loss of
five of their members to Willem of Turol more or less signaled the end of
the guild. It was quite sad. You can still visit Turolopolis, you know,
though it is merely ruins now.&+g"&N
~
M
cimmeria~
&+g"&+wThat was an extremely interesting part of my life,&+g" Dromis says. "&+wFor a time
I nearly considered leaving my work as a sage to study the Master's Path of
Winduin. Common sense prevailed, though, and I continued my writing. They
don't need recruits, at any rate. They have twelve thriving colonies now,
moving across Duris and teaching the ways of Winduin. Although I seem to
remember hearing recently that one of the colonies is in some sort of
trouble...&+g"
&+gDromis trails off and looks into the distance, trying to remember.&N
~
M
fonstaf~
